## Independent acceptance closure

`Verify and close` authorizes closure only after a fresh evidence-backed PASS; it is not a
timeout-based approval. `fixed`/`verified` alone never authorizes closure.
`Commit=false` permits checking the uncommitted deliverable, not assuming it is committed.

{{ if .Session.IsChild -}}
This session cannot spawn children. Delegate to parent `{{ .Session.ParentID }}` with
`mitto_conversation_send_prompt(self_id: "{{ .Session.ID }}", conversation_id: "{{ .Session.ParentID }}",
prompt: "<the complete Acceptance closure coordinator section below, with the effective ticket ID substituted>")`.
Send the whole procedure, not a request to run Start work (the parent may be linked to another ticket).
Tell the parent that terminal labels do NOT permit closing/reaping this work before this gate finishes.
Record the handoff on the effective ticket. If the parent supplied wait/report instructions,
call `mitto_children_tasks_report` with its task_id, status `verification_pending`, and the handoff
summary so its worker wait can finish; this is not acceptance PASS. Then end the turn without
closing or deleting yourself.
If the handoff fails or the parent cannot coordinate, report it and leave the ticket open.
The following section is for that parent to execute, not for this child to self-verify.
{{- else -}}
Execute the coordinator section below in this conversation. Do not queue Start work again.
{{- end }}

### Acceptance closure coordinator

You own verification and closure of **<effective-id> only**, not your own linked ticket or its parent.
Use `{{ if .Session.IsChild }}{{ .Session.ParentID }}{{ else }}{{ .Session.ID }}{{ end }}` as your `self_id`.
The caller's Commit={{ ne .Args.Commit "false" }} policy remains in force; this handoff grants no
new commit permission. Requested commits/checks must already be finished by the worker.
This is one bounded verification attempt, not a repair loop. Do not run implementation or Start work
inline. Do not close from terminal labels, prior comments, a stopped child, or the wait tool's
`success`/`completed` wrapper.

1. Reload the effective ticket, children and blockers. If closed, report and stop. If blocked,
   deferred, future `defer_until`, `needs-human`, children remain open, or human/external sign-off is required, leave open.
   Confirm the terminal label is `fixed` (bug) or `verified` (feature/task/chore); otherwise leave open.
   If implementation workers are still editing this tree, leave open rather than racing or polling.
   Do not bypass those requirements. If requested commits/checks are unfinished, leave open;
   make no commits after the snapshot.
2. Generate a unique `<attempt-id>` (UUID). Capture `<state>` as a compact JSON string with keys
   `workspace`, `head`, `ticket_sha256`, `tree_sha256`. The ticket hash covers ID, title, description,
   design, acceptance criteria, non-report comments, type, status, `defer_until`, labels,
   child/blocker IDs and statuses: canonical
   JSON (sorted keys, sorted label/relationship lists). The tree hash covers staged and unstaged
   binary diffs plus sorted untracked paths AND file contents (length-prefix the components).
   `git status` alone is insufficient. Exclude bookkeeping timestamps and ONLY this attempt's
   own pending/report comments, not other comments that can change requirements/evidence.
   Forward the exact hashing recipe with the snapshot so
   the verifier can reproduce it; inability to reproduce it is UNKNOWN, never an assumed match.
   Record `Acceptance pending: <attempt-id>` on the ticket. Never reuse an earlier PASS.
3. Spawn a fresh, non-looping child, in this same workspace:
   ```
   mitto_conversation_new(
     self_id: "<coordinator-id>", title: "Acceptance: <effective-id> <attempt-id>",
     beads_issue: "<effective-id>", prompt_name: "Acceptance verification phase",
     model_tag: "Reasoning",
     arguments: { "IssueID": "<effective-id>", "AttemptID": "<attempt-id>", "ExpectedState": "<state>", "SnapshotRecipe": "<exact commands/normalization used>" }
   )
   ```
   The phase declares no reuse/singleton target. Require a NEW conversation ID: a reused/coalesced
   response or permission/model/spawn error means leave open, notify, stop. Never verify inline.
4. Wait using `mitto_children_tasks_wait(self_id: "<coordinator-id>", children_list: ["<verifier-id>"],
   task_id: "<attempt-id>", timeout_seconds: 600)`. Omit `prompt`: the phase already carries its
   report instructions; do not queue duplicate verifier turns. Timeout, missing/malformed report, tool error, synthetic `stuck`,
   `not_running`, failed or UNKNOWN result: leave open, record the reason and notify. End this
   attempt without retrying, repairing, or requeueing Start work. Keep a still-running verifier
   and its coordinator conversation alive; never delete them on timeout.
5. Accept only the actual designated child's report with matching issue ID, attempt ID and state,
   verdict PASS, a non-empty criterion checklist, EVERY criterion PASS with concrete evidence,
   and no blockers. Reload the durable `Acceptance verification:` report on the ticket and require
   it to agree. FAIL, UNKNOWN, skipped criteria, inferred/ambiguous requirements, or absent evidence
    leaves the ticket open; preserve whether UNKNOWN is due to evidence, scope, stale state, or
    another cause; do not label uncertainty a confirmed external blocker. Record findings, notify,
    and stop. Do not turn mandatory remaining work
   into follow-up tickets merely to obtain PASS.
6. Immediately recapture the state from step 2 (same narrowly defined exclusions) and compare it;
   recheck children/blockers, deferral/human gates and completion labels. Any change/unknown invalidates this attempt:
   leave open and report stale verification; do not silently start another attempt.
   Only an unchanged PASS permits:
   `bd close <effective-id> --reason "Acceptance PASS <attempt-id>: <evidence summary>"`.
   Check command success and reload status before announcing closure. Record/notify errors explicitly.
   Never push or close another ticket. Clean up only this attempt's finished verifier AFTER its
   report is durable. Report the outcome to the requesting child if this was a delegated handoff;
   do not reap that worker until the outcome is recorded.

This is a prompt-level contract, not a transactional lock against concurrent writers. If concurrent
edits cannot be excluded or the snapshot cannot be captured reliably, return UNKNOWN and leave open.
